Let $S=S_1 \cap S_2 \cap S_3$ where:
$$
\begin{aligned}
& \cdot S_1=\{z|z \in C,| z \mid < 4\} \\
& \cdot S_2=\left\{z \mid z \in C, I_m\left(\frac{z-1+i \sqrt{3}}{1-i \sqrt{3}}\right)>0\right\} \\
& \cdot S_3=\{z \mid z \in C, R(z)>0\}
\end{aligned}
$$
If the area of $S$ can be expressed as $\frac{a}{b} \pi$, where $a$ and $b$ are positive integers that are relatively prime. Find $a+b$.

